        "title": "fix(ui): make tabs, dialogs, and skill cards keyboard accessible",
        "body": "Related: #106266\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes issues where keyboard and assistive-technology users could not reliably skip navigation, activate tabbed settings, open skill cards, or dismiss and focus shared dialogs.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdds a native skip link, shared keyboard tab behavior, correct tab and panel relationships, native skill-card actions, and stronger shared modal focus/dismissal behavior. This is the dependency-free accessibility foundation before the Web Awesome component migration.\n\n## User Impact\n\nUsers can reach main content immediately, move through tabs with Arrow, Home, and End keys, activate skill cards without pointer-only behavior, and use consistent modal focus, Escape, and backdrop dismissal.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Blacksmith Testbox run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29243845709\n- UI unit/browser suite: 238 files and 3,781 tests passed.\n- Changed gate passed, including UI typecheck, formatting, and lint.\n- Production Control UI build passed.\n- Changed-surface mocked Gateway E2E: 4/4 passed, including skip navigation and keyboard tab activation.\n- Full UI E2E: 160/166 passed. The six failures are outside this diff: four current expectation/runtime drifts reproduced in isolated reruns, one native-session timing failure passed on isolated rerun, and one stale sidebar expectation follows the newly added Devices route on current main.\n- Fresh autoreview: no accepted or actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted implementation; maintainer-directed and independently tested.\n",
